const sections = [["operator", "Operator"], ["local", "Local data and AI providers"], ["analytics", "Analytics"], ["services", "Website, downloads and support"], ["choices", "Retention and your choices"], ["contact", "Security, children and contact"]] as const;
---
<LegalPage title="Privacy Policy - Doer" description="Doer's local storage, AI-provider requests, analytics and privacy choices." heading="Doer Privacy Policy" lede="Doer runs on your computer and uses the AI providers you connect. This policy describes information stored locally and sent to external services." effectiveDate="2026-10-07" lastUpdated="2026-10-07" sections={sections}>
  <section id="operator"><h2>Operator</h2><p>Doer and <a href="https://doer.lagaryan.click">doer.lagaryan.click</a> are operated by Aryan Gupta and Aditya Mayank Sinha in India. The Microsoft Store publisher display name is Baandra. Privacy and support requests: <a href="mailto:aryan@lagaryan.click">aryan@lagaryan.click</a>. Doer is an independent fork of MIT-licensed T3 Code. T3 Tools, Inc. is the upstream copyright holder, not Doer's operator.</p></section>
  <section id="local"><h2>Local data and AI providers</h2><p>Tasks, messages, attachments, history, instructions, schedules, settings and provider credentials are stored on the computer running Doer's server. Doer does not automatically upload the local task database or credentials to its operator. The app can read and write your selected folders and run provider command-line tools. Devices you pair may access the host's tasks and enabled tools; pair only devices you trust. Your chosen remote host and network services have their own data practices.</p><p>Your chosen AI provider receives prompts, attached or referenced file contents, conversation context and tool results needed for a task. Providers may include OpenAI/Codex, Anthropic/Claude, Cursor, xAI/Grok, OpenCode and other services you connect. Their account, subscription, privacy, retention and data-use terms apply separately. Review them before sharing sensitive information. Doer does not operate an AI backend that keeps a separate server-side copy of your tasks.</p></section>
  <section id="analytics"><h2>Analytics</h2><p>Doer 0.0.56 enables product analytics by default using PostHog's US cloud service. Events include feature usage, provider and model, app version, platform, architecture, turn status and duration, token totals and error reports. An installation or browser identifier associates events with the same installation. Analytics event code does not intentionally include prompts, AI responses, file contents or authentication tokens.</p><p>The browser SDK also records interactions, page views, errors and session recordings. Form inputs are masked and query strings and fragments are removed from recorded page URLs. Other rendered content, including task or file content visible on screen, can appear in recordings. Recordings are not limited to anonymous aggregate statistics.</p><p>Set <code>T3CODE_TELEMETRY_ENABLED=false</code> in the host's environment before starting Doer to disable server and browser analytics. The browser SDK also honors Do Not Track. Hosts may configure a different PostHog service and are responsible for that configuration. Analytics is used to understand usage and investigate problems, not to sell information or target advertising.</p></section>
  <section id="services"><h2>Website, downloads and support</h2><p>Direct downloads and updates use GitHub and our download host; matching command-line packages use npm. The Microsoft Store build receives app updates through Microsoft Store. These services receive network information such as IP addresses and requested downloads or versions. Website hosting and delivery services, including Vercel and Cloudflare, process IP addresses and HTTP request details to serve the site and maintain security.</p><p>Emailing us shares your email address and message contents. We use correspondence to respond, investigate issues and meet legal obligations. Remove credentials and sensitive task contents from shared logs. We may disclose information when required by law or to protect rights and security.</p></section>
  <section id="choices"><h2>Retention and your choices</h2><p>Local tasks, history, settings and credentials remain until you delete them. Uninstalling may leave local application data, typically under <code>%USERPROFILE%\.doer</code>. Delete that data separately if you want to remove it; operating-system backups may retain copies. External providers retain copies according to their own policies.</p><p>PostHog events and recordings follow the analytics project's configured retention settings. Contact us for applicable retention details or to request deletion of information associated with your installation. Disabling analytics stops future collection; it does not delete existing events or recordings. Support information is kept as needed to handle the request and legal obligations.</p><p>You can choose providers, disconnect services, revoke paired devices and delete local data. Depending on your location, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, restrict or object to processing, or obtain a copy of personal information. Contact us for information held by the operator and your chosen provider for information it holds.</p></section>
  <section id="contact"><h2>Security, children and contact</h2><p>Doer uses operating-system-protected secret storage where supported and HTTPS for external service requests. No storage or transmission method is completely secure. The operators are based in India; PostHog's default service processes analytics in the United States, and other providers may process information elsewhere.</p><p>Doer is not directed to children under 13. Contact us if a child has supplied personal information to the operator. We update this policy when practices change and revise the date above.</p><p>Privacy and support: Aryan Gupta, <a href="mailto:aryan@lagaryan.click">aryan@lagaryan.click</a>; Aditya Mayank Sinha, <a href="mailto:adityamayank708@gmail.com">adityamayank708@gmail.com</a>.</p></section>
</LegalPage>
